set-algorithm-set-pp-command: TPM2_SetAlgorithmSet can be gated with Physical Presence

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 1, version 185, "Physical Presence
Authorization"): "If, in Part 3, the schematic for a command has
`TPM_RH_PLATFORM` in the "Description" column for one of the handles, then
that command can be added to the list of commands that require PP."; Part 3,
TPM2_PP_Commands: "Only commands with handle types of `TPMI_RH_PLATFORM`,
`TPMI_RH_PROVISION`, `TPMI_RH_CLEAR`, or `TPMI_RH_HIERARCHY` can be gated with
Physical Presence. If any other command is in either list, it is discarded."

TPM2_SetAlgorithmSet authorizes `authHandle`, a `TPMI_RH_PLATFORM` whose
Description is `TPM_RH_PLATFORM`, but the reference's command attribute table
lacks PP_COMMAND for it, so TPM2_PP_Commands silently discards it and it never
appears in TPM_CAP_PP_COMMANDS (the TCG reference version 185 has
PP_COMMAND). The patch adds PP_COMMAND to its attributes.
diff --git a/src/CommandAttributeData.h b/src/CommandAttributeData.h
--- a/src/CommandAttributeData.h
+++ b/src/CommandAttributeData.h
@@ -613,7 +613,11 @@ const COMMAND_ATTRIBUTES    s_commandAttributes [] = {
 #endif
 #if (PAD_LIST  || CC_SetAlgorithmSet)
     (COMMAND_ATTRIBUTES)(CC_SetAlgorithmSet             *  // 0x013f
-			 (IS_IMPLEMENTED+HANDLE_1_USER)),
+			 // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+			 // determinism): authHandle is a TPMI_RH_PLATFORM, so the command
+			 // can be gated with Physical Presence (Part 1, "Physical Presence
+			 // Authorization"; Part 3, TPM2_PP_Commands).
+			 (IS_IMPLEMENTED+HANDLE_1_USER+PP_COMMAND)),
 #endif
 #if (PAD_LIST  || CC_SetCommandCodeAuditStatus)
     (COMMAND_ATTRIBUTES)(CC_SetCommandCodeAuditStatus   *  // 0x0140
